WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 1.4 · Strategic Foundations
Values in practice

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Values set early shape the culture of everything you build.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
Values are the principles that guide what you do when decisions are hard. A single word is only a start: describe what people will actually do, and how you would notice it.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
Each value in three lines

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:37.130
What it means: One sentence on what the value means for you. For example: Respect: every trainee is treated as a colleague, whatever their school record.

6
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:48.459
How it shows: What you will actually do, and what it costs in time and money. For example: We budget for mentor time and pay trainees from their very first shift.

7
00:00:48.459 --> 00:00:59.137
What you avoid: The behaviour the value rules out, even under pressure. For example: We never use trainees as unpaid help to cover a busy Saturday.

8
00:00:59.537 --> 00:01:00.137
Why they matter

9
00:01:00.137 --> 00:01:05.441
1. They guide you when there is no rule to follow.

10
00:01:05.441 --> 00:01:10.744
2. Values set early shape the culture of everything you build.

11
00:01:10.744 --> 00:01:17.048
3. Agreeing them now prevents conflict at your first hard decision.

12
00:01:17.448 --> 00:01:18.048
What they guide

13
00:01:18.048 --> 00:01:23.352
1. How you handle difficult decisions you can foresee this year.

14
00:01:23.352 --> 00:01:28.656
2. Your first budget, because practising values costs time and money.

15
00:01:28.656 --> 00:01:34.219
3. Your code of conduct, later in the course.

16
00:01:34.619 --> 00:01:35.219
What to avoid

17
00:01:35.219 --> 00:01:39.781
Adopting values only because other organisations display them.

18
00:01:39.781 --> 00:01:44.715
Too many: keep three to five you can practise.

19
00:01:44.715 --> 00:01:50.278
Ignoring trade-offs, such as openness against participants’ privacy.

20
00:01:50.878 --> 00:01:52.678
You write three to five values and test them on a hard decision.

21
00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:56.678
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:01:58.178 --> 00:02:01.278
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
